causal-loop 1

# Is a Business Philosophy study applicable at a university of applied sciences?
#
# Written for this repository. A university of applied sciences is judged by
# what its graduates can do in practice, and philosophy is easily heard as the
# opposite of that. This diagram does not answer the question with a yes or a
# no. It shows the feedback that decides it: the loops that make such a study
# more applicable the longer it runs, and the loops that quietly work against
# it. Nothing here is simulated; the weights are annotations.
#
# The study's own stance is in the model too. It does not promise concrete
# solutions to wicked problems such as polarization, climate change or social
# and mental wellbeing. It promises more and better insight into them, and the
# loops below say why that is the more applicable promise, not the less.
#
# The arrangement is authored: the positions are in the .adp beside this file,
# and three links are flipped so that their arcs pass clear of the loop labels.

# ---- variables ---------------------------------------------------------------

variable applicability "Applicability in practice"
variable fieldEngagement "Engagement of organizations"
variable expertDiversity "Diversity of expertise"
variable insight "Depth of shared insight"
variable practicalTools "Practical tools in use"
variable practiceGap "Distance from daily practice"
variable openInquiry "Room for open inquiry"
variable recipeUse "Tools used as recipes"
variable coreValues "Curiosity, transparency, ethics"
variable philosophy "Philosophical depth"
variable trust "Trust and openness"
variable latentWisdom "Latent wisdom made explicit"
variable narratives "Stories and narratives"
variable polarization "Polarization"
variable creativeExpression "Art and creative expression"
variable communicationRange "Communication beyond words"
variable wickedProblems "Weight of wicked problems"
variable quickFixPressure "Pressure for quick solutions"

# ---- the field comes to the study --------------------------------------------
# Organizations notice when graduates make a difference, and they bring their
# cases, their people and their questions. Experts from different disciplines
# and practices look at the same case from different sides, which is where
# insight comes from. The delay is the point: a reputation in the professional
# field is built over cohorts, not over a semester.

link insight -> applicability + weight=1.2
link applicability -> fieldEngagement + delayed "a reputation is built over cohorts"
link fieldEngagement -> expertDiversity + "practitioners, guest lecturers, other disciplines"
link expertDiversity -> insight + flipped

loop R1 "Relevance draws the field" applicability fieldEngagement expertDiversity insight

# ---- tools: the bridge and the trap ------------------------------------------
# Organizations ask for something they can use on Monday morning. Practical
# tools - dialogue formats, value mapping, Socratic conversation, scenario
# thinking - translate philosophical ideas into work, and so close the distance
# to daily practice. Two negative links, an even count: this is reinforcing.
#
# The same tools, applied mechanically, become recipes, and a recipe replaces
# the thinking it was meant to support. One negative link: balancing. The
# more the field asks for tools, the more this loop holds the study back.

link fieldEngagement -> practicalTools +
link practicalTools -> practiceGap - flipped "tools translate ideas into work"
link practiceGap -> insight - flipped "insight stays in the classroom"

loop R2 "Tools translate thinking" applicability fieldEngagement practicalTools practiceGap insight

link practicalTools -> recipeUse +
link recipeUse -> insight - flipped weight=0.8 "a recipe replaces the thinking"

loop B1 "The toolkit trap" applicability fieldEngagement practicalTools recipeUse insight

# ---- values and the philosophers ---------------------------------------------
# Every insight raises a better question. Curiosity sends students to the
# philosophers and their streams of thought - virtue ethics, pragmatism,
# phenomenology, systems thinking - which give them new lenses on a case.
#
# Depth has a price: the further a stream of thought is from the shop floor,
# the harder it is to share what it shows. One negative link, so this is the
# balancing loop that keeps philosophical depth honest.

link insight -> coreValues + "every answer raises a better question"
link coreValues -> philosophy +
link philosophy -> insight + flipped "philosophers lend new lenses"

loop R3 "Questions deepen" insight coreValues philosophy

link philosophy -> practiceGap + delayed

loop B2 "Depth drifts from practice" insight coreValues philosophy practiceGap

# ---- the wisdom organizations already have -----------------------------------
# Organizations know more than they can say. Transparency and ethics make it
# safe to say it; latent wisdom surfaces as stories, and stories carry insight
# that a report cannot.

link coreValues -> trust + flipped
link trust -> latentWisdom +
link latentWisdom -> narratives + "wisdom travels as stories"
link narratives -> insight +

loop R4 "Openness surfaces wisdom" insight coreValues trust latentWisdom narratives

# ---- wicked problems and the divide ------------------------------------------
# Polarization closes the conversation in which latent wisdom could surface.
# Shared stories make the other side recognizable again. Two negative links:
# reinforcing, as a vicious circle when polarization rises and a virtuous one
# when stories win.

link wickedProblems -> polarization + "climate, wellbeing, identity"
link polarization -> trust -
link narratives -> polarization -

loop R5 "Stories soften the divide" trust latentWisdom narratives polarization

# ---- more than text and voice ------------------------------------------------
# Not everything worth saying fits in words. Images, theatre, music and making
# things let people express what they cannot yet argue, and are heard across
# lines where arguments are not.

link trust -> creativeExpression + flipped "safe enough to show, not only tell"
link creativeExpression -> communicationRange + flipped
link communicationRange -> polarization - flipped "heard across lines where arguments are not"

loop R6 "Art speaks across divides" trust creativeExpression communicationRange polarization

# ---- insight rather than solutions -------------------------------------------
# Wicked problems create pressure for a quick, concrete solution. That
# pressure eats the room for open inquiry, and it is the room for inquiry that
# produces insight. Insight in turn eases the pressure, slowly, by showing why
# the quick solution would not have worked. Two negative links: reinforcing.
#
# Under pressure, tools also get applied as recipes. Again two negative links,
# again reinforcing: the hurry that recipes come from is fed by the shallow
# insight they produce.

link wickedProblems -> quickFixPressure + flipped
link quickFixPressure -> openInquiry - "no time for questions without answers"
link openInquiry -> insight + weight=1.5
link insight -> quickFixPressure - delayed "insight shows why the quick fix fails"

loop R7 "Haste narrows the view" insight quickFixPressure openInquiry

link quickFixPressure -> recipeUse + flipped

loop R8 "Recipes for the impatient" insight quickFixPressure recipeUse
